{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793002035,"nonce":"vA2eprggKmWQFFW9BFVl5kc/D7o=","title":"Open build settings before scanning workspace folders","message":"BuildSettings synchronously located the main class, checked class paths and recursively scanned candidate source directories during rendering. In a remote workspace this multiplied filesystem RPCs and could hold the UI for about a minute. Move metadata and suggestions to a cancellable data-only worker, cap the traversal, skip generated directories, and render controls immediately with lookup loading/failure feedback. Deliver only completed results at the UI frame boundary and stop work when the view closes.\n\nValidation: BuildLookupChecks holds the provider indefinitely while asserting the form's controls already exist and no filesystem call ran on the UI thread; releasing it updates the main-class result. The existing SettingsChecks suite passes. The full browser navigation fixture delays filesystem listing and captures the complete build form with checking indicators before the scan returns. Updated bundle staged in bin/web/rayde.\n\nThe explicit worker comparator also avoids the current Ash hybrid-worker unprepared-JIT sentinel reached through Reflect.compare; browser AOT and native hybrid checks now pass.","files":null}]}